1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
The End

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
The End

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The End

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Shoo!

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Aaaaaah!

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Iko!

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Ha ha ha ha ha!

8
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
One bear successfully eliminated by our trap!

9
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
We know what you two really are and this is what you get!

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
From the beginning, we hated you.

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
But also we loved you from the beginning as well.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
All we wanted was to become true friends with you.

13
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
So we had to cross the wall.

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
I had to have you all to myself.

15
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Tomorrow's the day.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Oh, Sumika.

17
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
What was it you wanted to tell me?

18
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Kirikuma!

19
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Kirikuma Hiroshi!

20
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:35,580
This letter is hard. I barely even know what to say.

21
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:46,020
I guess I can start at the beginning. The moment I first met Kureha, I'll never forget that day.

22
00:02:55,020 --> 00:03:01,200
Oh no! It's gone! I can't find it!

23
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:08,400
Grandma gave me that hairpin especially for today. I can't believe I lost it.

24
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:11,200
Are you looking for this?

25
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:13,060
Here.

26
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:18,420
It's yours, right?

27
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:21,720
Yes, thank you.

28
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:29,940
I know you probably don't remember that, but I do. And it meant the world to me.

29
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:34,120
I was so happy you were there. So happy to have met you.

30
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:42,540
And then, there was that storm. And I wanted to protect what you cared about.

31
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,900
You came out too!

32
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:56,300
We got soaked, remember? Sure, it was scary, but we ended up having such a good time.

33
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:04,680
I started feeling so close to you. Like it was just you and me. The only two people in the whole world.

34
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:09,020
It was heaven. I remember everything about that day.

35
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:15,160
But more importantly, I will always remember it, even when I'm old and gray.

36
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:25,760
The Moon Girl and the Forest Girl. Your mother wrote this?

37
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:28,660
Yep. It was actually her last book.

38
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:33,380
Since it was never published, it's the only copy. It's so good.

39
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:35,160
Mind if I read it?

40
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:36,120
Not at all.

41
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:45,280
Once upon a time, the worlds were divided into two parts by the sky.

42
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:49,260
There was the moon world and the forest world.

43
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:54,100
One day, a moon girl accidentally dropped her mother's precious pendant.

44
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:56,700
It fell far down into the forest.

45
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:01,240
A forest girl stumbled upon the pendant while she was out walking.

46
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:08,660
Surprised by its sparkling star, she found herself looking up at the sky to see where it came from.

47
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:13,920
She started to think what she could see might not be all there was and said,

48
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,560
There must be an amazing world beyond that sky.

49
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:24,980
Meanwhile, the moon girl couldn't stop wondering about the forest world and what happened to the pendant.

50
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:27,900
Where is mother's pendant, she said.

51
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:32,880
I have to go find it. There must be an amazing world beyond that sky.

52
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:40,800
Day after day, the moon girl and the forest girl looked at the sky, each one gazing from their own world.

53
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:48,540
At long last, they decided to appeal to Lady Kumaria, for she was the goddess of the sky.

54
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:51,500
The moon girl prayed,

55
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,840
Please help me, Lady Kumaria.

56
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:59,440
I want to go beyond the sky, so I can find my mother's lost pendant.

57
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:01,800
The forest girl prayed,

58
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:04,020
Please help me, Lady Kumaria.

59
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:10,220
I want to go beyond the sky, so I can deliver this lost star to the one who dropped it.

60
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:16,240
I am sorry, but you may not, said Kumaria, for the two worlds have been severed forever.

61
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:22,140
Wanting to cross that severance is pride, and pride, as you know, is a grave sin.

62
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:25,040
And yet they prayed again,

63
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:29,000
Please help us, we still want to go beyond the sky.

64
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:32,920
Reluctantly, Kumaria answered them,

65
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:37,960
There is one way to make your wish come true.

66
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:43,600
In the center of the sky is a place called the Door to Friendship.

67
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:47,040
If your love is true,

68
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,240
Your friend will be waiting for you.

69
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:52,420
You'll find her on the other side of that door.

70
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,860
When you see her, give her a promise kiss.

71
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:59,300
Do that, and your wish shall come true.

72
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:03,160
Kumaria asked the two girls a question,

73
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:06,460
Is your love the real thing?

74
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:10,620
Then she laid down a ladder for them,

75
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:13,700
Connecting the two worlds together once more.

76
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:18,960
They climbed the ladder until finally arriving at the center of the sky.

77
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:25,780
There they found a single, vast mirror standing like a wall in their path.

78
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:30,020
Each girl saw her own reflection in the mirror.

79
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:34,480
They heard Kumaria's voice say,

80
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:39,740
Now your friend is waiting just on the other side of that very door.

81
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:43,420
If you smash the you in the mirror to bits,

82
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:45,500
If you tear yourself apart,

83
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:48,200
She shall grant you a promised kiss.

84
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,560
But beware,

85
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,920
This may cost you your life.

86
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:56,200
I will ask you one more time,

87
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:58,600
Is your love the real thing?

88
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:04,480
The girls stared at themselves in the mirror for a very long time.

89
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:09,520
Is that the end?

90
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:12,040
No, the story doesn't have an ending.

91
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:13,780
A bear killed mom.

92
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:16,000
She never got the chance to finish it.

93
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,720
How sad.

94
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:23,100
So, what would you do if it was about you?

95
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:24,220
Uh...

96
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:26,320
You know, that part in the story.

97
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,720
Would you risk your life in order to break the mirror?

98
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,180
I'm not really sure.

99
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:32,820
Let me think.

100
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:34,440
I would break it.

101
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:34,940
What?

102
00:08:34,940 --> 00:08:40,320
I'd shoot my reflection.

103
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:44,920
I'd shoot.

104
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:47,920
Because I would do anything to prove my love was true.

105
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:50,620
In that moment,

106
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,740
I decided I wouldn't back down on love either.

107
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,720
No matter what happened.

108
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:59,720
I would do anything to prove my love too.

109
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:07,540
Now, ladies, it's time to decide on the next evil to exclude.

110
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:10,300
Let's search evil!

111
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:42,540
Oh, ladies, I have bad news.

112
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:44,580
It seems we have a traitor among our ranks.

113
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:47,880
Kurehatsu Baki was the one set up to be the next evil.

114
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,820
Unfortunately, before we can target her,

115
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,460
we must first exclude the traitor.

116
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:55,480
I'm sure she agrees.

117
00:09:55,740 --> 00:09:57,080
Right, Sumika Izumino?

118
00:09:57,080 --> 00:10:04,140
Kureha, I'm sorry.

119
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:06,360
I jumped into the storm myself,

120
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:07,780
and I did it willingly.

121
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:14,820
At the time,

122
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:17,300
I thought if I could prove my love,

123
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:19,220
I wouldn't mind getting hurt,

124
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:20,840
even heartbroken.

125
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:23,140
But then,

126
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:25,260
I realized I was wrong.

127
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:28,480
It wouldn't be me the Invisible Storm would break.

128
00:10:29,060 --> 00:10:30,680
It would wind up being you,

129
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:32,980
the one I care about most.

130
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:40,040
Good.

131
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,180
You wrote the letter.

132
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:44,240
Oh, Kauru.

133
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:44,760
Thanks.

134
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:45,480
Great work.

135
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:46,520
I can take it now.

136
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,340
That way, I'll be ready to give it to Kureha.

137
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:50,980
What's the problem?

138
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:52,920
About the letter,

139
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,180
would you mind holding off a bit?

140
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:59,000
I'd like to wait until we celebrate Kureha's birthday here,

141
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,120
at the garden.

142
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:02,640
Is that okay?

143
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:05,760
Fine, whatever.

144
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:07,360
Just don't forget,

145
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,720
I have to be Kureha's new friend.

146
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:13,500
That's the only way we can make sure the storm will pass her by.

147
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:14,720
Yeah.

148
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:17,160
I can't stop the storm,

149
00:11:17,620 --> 00:11:19,320
but I can protect Kureha,

150
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:21,420
as long as I'm her new friend.

151
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:24,540
I know it puts you in a terrible position,

152
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,940
but we have no other choice if we want to save her.

153
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:35,220
I still think I should do it.

154
00:11:35,620 --> 00:11:36,780
Deliver the letter, I mean.

155
00:11:37,180 --> 00:11:37,540
No.

156
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:38,920
Let me.

157
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,400
This is the last love I ever get to give her,

158
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:42,760
so it has to be done right.

159
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,140
It has to be me.

160
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:45,760
Okay.

161
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:48,260
Thank you.

162
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,460
I appreciate it.

163
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:50,540
See ya.

164
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:58,380
Kureha.

165
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:01,080
This will be my present to you,

166
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,800
because I understand now.

167
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:15,800
I promise to never back down on love.

168
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:29,080
I owe you one.

169
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:31,200
Thank you for saving my life.

170
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:34,540
You told me the truth about Ginko and Lulu,

171
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:36,840
that they were bears disguised as humans.

172
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,320
Because of you,

173
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:40,040
I got to set a trap in advance.

174
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:42,200
Although...

175
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:45,220
We know what you are,

176
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:46,280
and this is what you get!

177
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,260
Bear Flash!

178
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:57,300
I can't believe that stupid bear,

179
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:59,100
who knew she'd have a trick up her sleeve.

180
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:01,920
But it's not a problem.

181
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:03,760
The plane is still going off without a hitch.

182
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:06,500
Yes, Sumika's death was definitely unexpected,

183
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:09,020
but your idea of using it was inspired.

184
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,160
Pure genius.

185
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,980
Tomorrow, it'll finally be Kureha Tsubaki's birthday,

186
00:13:13,980 --> 00:13:16,900
and I think we'll really enjoy it.

187
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:25,200
Oh, no.

188
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,560
Don't tell me.

189
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,360
Leave me alone, for your own sake!

190
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:38,560
I wonder where they could have gone.

191
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:41,720
I was planning to apologize, too.

192
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:43,720
Growl!

193
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:45,200
Ginko!

194
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:48,800
Oh, hang in there!

195
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,940
Growl, sniffle!

196
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,360
Dang it!

197
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:54,140
Stupid Kaoru, Harishima!

198
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:56,140
It doesn't make any sense!

199
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,440
How did she even know we were bears?

200
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:06,340
Reya,

201
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:11,140
I can't help but be reminded of the day I swore my love to you.

202
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:14,980
And now, it's your daughter's turn.

203
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:18,700
I wonder what she'll get from her friend on her birthday.

204
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:32,920
So that it's perfect, since it's my present to you.

205
00:14:34,420 --> 00:14:34,860
Sumika,

206
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:37,300
I promise to accept your gift,

207
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:39,260
and I'll do what you asked me to.

208
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:39,660
Hmm.

209
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:43,140
Hey, Kureha,

210
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:45,840
do you remember the day of the entrance ceremony?

211
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:46,880
What?

212
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:50,780
Pummeled by the cold wind that scattered the cherry blossoms.

213
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:54,900
A girl searched for something, but she couldn't seem to find it.

214
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:58,600
I felt bad for Sumika.

215
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:01,160
No one helped her look for it at all.

216
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:03,140
Although, why would they?

217
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:06,400
It was just some cheap hairpin, nothing to get upset about.

218
00:15:07,180 --> 00:15:09,500
But you, you're not like the rest of us.

219
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:14,140
Tell me something.

220
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:16,520
Why haven't you lost hope yet?

221
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,820
The world is cruel.

222
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:20,480
You've lost things,

223
00:15:20,740 --> 00:15:21,880
had them taken from you.

224
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,620
Why don't you become invisible?

225
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:24,680
Well,

226
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:28,640
I think it's because I don't forget love.

227
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:31,060
I don't understand what that means.

228
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:32,820
It means,

229
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,660
as long as you don't forget love,

230
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:36,020
you'll never, ever be alone.

231
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,920
And if you don't give up on love,

232
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:39,620
even if you lose something,

233
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:40,960
you won't be invisible.

234
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:43,480
What's that?

235
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:45,400
It's a letter from Sumika.

236
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:48,040
She gave it to me not too long ago.

237
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:49,280
This,

238
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:51,300
this is my birthday present.

239
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,720
I'm supposed to read it at the flower bed.

240
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:55,620
So, Kureha,

241
00:15:55,820 --> 00:15:57,540
it means a lot that you're giving us a chance

242
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:58,780
to make amends for all this.

243
00:15:58,980 --> 00:15:59,460
Thank you.

244
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:03,280
I'm super excited about your birthday party, aren't you?

245
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:04,740
Yes, I am.

246
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,360
Thank you.

247
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,740
Oh, there's no need to thank me, silly.

248
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:10,560
Especially considering your love

249
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:12,360
is about to be utterly destroyed

250
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:14,060
by the invisible storm.

251
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:18,940
Kureha!

252
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:20,160
Kureha!

253
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:22,000
Ginko, you're alive!

254
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:24,260
Oh, Lulu's so happy, Ginko!

255
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:25,300
What a relief!

256
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:26,560
That was terrifying!

257
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,000
Lulu was so worried!

258
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:30,080
She didn't know what she'd do if you died!

259
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:32,100
Lulu did everything she could think of!

260
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:34,080
She carried you all the way to here

261
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,300
and stayed up the whole night

262
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:36,580
taking care of you!

263
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:37,140
Oh, no!

264
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:38,660
Today is Kureha's birthday!

265
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:40,420
Growl, growl, growl!

266
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:40,920
Huh?

267
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:43,100
I said today is Kureha's birthday!

268
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:43,420
Huh?

269
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:43,740
Huh?

270
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:44,020
Huh?

271
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:44,120
Huh?

272
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:49,520
Hello?

273
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,040
Is your love the real thing?

274
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:55,240
This is a challenge from the Wall of Severance.

275
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:56,900
Ginko, Yurishiro,

276
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:58,640
if your love is true,

277
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,840
you need to get to the flower bed.

278
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:03,000
The moon girl is there right now

279
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,100
awaiting your arrival.

280
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,180
Do I know a moon girl?

281
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:09,120
All you have to do is give yourself over to the flames.

282
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,320
Only then will your love be approved.

283
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:12,160
Kureha!

284
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:13,740
Are you trying to tell me

285
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:15,520
the moon girl is supposed to be Kureha?

286
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:18,020
All right.

287
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:19,740
I wonder if the promised kiss

288
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:20,820
will come to pass now.

289
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:21,820
We shall see.

290
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:23,600
For that is sexy.

291
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:25,260
Shabba da do.

292
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:44,520
On your birthday, Kureha.

293
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:45,740
We wish you well.

294
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:46,880
Happy birthday!

295
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:50,620
Thank you, guys.

296
00:17:52,420 --> 00:17:53,920
Don't forget your promise.

297
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:56,580
You told Sumika you'd read her letter right here.

298
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:57,800
Yeah.

299
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:02,880
Kureha,

300
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:05,120
the girl standing in front of you

301
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:06,260
is...

302
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:07,520
is your new friend.

303
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,900
What does this mean?

304
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:12,360
Exactly what it says.

305
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:15,220
It's pretty obvious when you think about it.

306
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:17,080
That's Sumika's breakup letter to you.

307
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:20,320
Seems she's trying to give you a gift, too.

308
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:22,160
Her final present for you

309
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,020
was to make sure you had a new friend.

310
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:25,660
One that wasn't her.

311
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:27,840
But we have no intention

312
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:29,000
of making friends with you,

313
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:30,020
Kureha Tsubaki.

314
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:32,140
I can't imagine it feels very good

315
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:33,640
to realize you were both tricked.

316
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:34,760
We were tricked?

317
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:36,040
That's right.

318
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:36,840
Surprise.

319
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:39,060
I was the one who had Sumika

320
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:39,880
write the letter to you

321
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,780
in the first place.

322
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:44,540
Her death screwed up

323
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,560
the original plan.

324
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:46,560
Yet fortunately,

325
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:47,760
we got to use that letter

326
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:49,400
to punish the real evil anyway.

327
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:50,780
The girl who refuses

328
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:52,240
to follow social cues.

329
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,340
In order to wish you

330
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:55,480
the happiest of birthdays,

331
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:56,460
Kureha Tsubaki,

332
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:58,540
this is a little something special

333
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,740
from us to you.

334
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:02,900
Happy birthday!

335
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:11,440
The time has come

336
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,940
for us to exclude the evil.

337
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:14,020
Exclude!

338
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:16,840
Tell me,

339
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:17,780
does evil get to have

340
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:18,360
any friends?

341
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:19,760
No friends!

342
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:22,100
Tell me,

343
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:23,140
does evil get crushed,

344
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:24,680
crushed by the invisible storm

345
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:25,280
as punishment?

346
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:26,920
Crush as punishment!

347
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:33,140
She's excluded!

348
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:34,440
Good job, ladies!

349
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:35,360
Kureha Tsubaki

350
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,600
just snapped like a twig!

351
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:37,080
Yay!

352
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:38,360
You did it!

353
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:39,900
Tragic.

354
00:19:40,460 --> 00:19:41,020
You won't get

355
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:41,980
any new friends.

356
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:43,480
On top of that,

357
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:44,280
you'll never be able

358
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:44,800
to accept

359
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:46,120
Sumika Izunino's

360
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:46,780
final gift.

361
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:48,280
Oh, what a pity.

362
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:49,680
At least now you know

363
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,600
the emotion of love

364
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:52,020
is powerless and pointless.

365
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,520
No use for this anymore!

366
00:19:55,520 --> 00:20:00,020
No, Sumika wrote that!

367
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:02,340
It's such a beautiful smile.

368
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,100
I want you to always

369
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:04,980
smile like that,

370
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:05,880
like a flower.

371
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,360
That's my love.

372
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:08,420
It's funny.

373
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,280
Even if I had to watch you

374
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:10,940
from a distance,

375
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:12,260
I would be happy

376
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:13,540
just to see that smile.

377
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,120
Please, it's Sumika's love!

378
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:17,680
She gave it to me!

379
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:22,280
Rell!

380
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:24,380
Oh, Kura!

381
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:30,780
What, Kinko?

382
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:35,340
Okay, everyone.

383
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:36,620
Looks like the party's over.

384
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:37,880
Let's get out of here!

385
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:38,920
Let's go!

386
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:39,580
We're on!

387
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:40,040
We're waiting!

388
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:42,120
Ah!

389
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:45,260
He won't!

390
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:47,340
He'll never back down on love!

391
00:20:47,340 --> 00:20:49,340
Kinko!

392
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:56,220
Ginko, you dummy!

393
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:57,340
Lulu would have killed you

394
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,680
if you'd really died this time!

395
00:20:58,780 --> 00:20:59,860
What were you thinking?

396
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:01,240
Why would you do that,

397
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:02,080
Ginko?

398
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:03,420
You're a dummy too!

399
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:04,980
She did it because she loves you!

400
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:06,260
She...

401
00:21:06,260 --> 00:21:07,680
She loves me?

402
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:08,800
That's right!

403
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:10,120
Ginko loves you so much!

404
00:21:10,180 --> 00:21:11,220
Look at what she's done!

405
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:12,120
For you!

406
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:18,880
Don't waste her love!

407
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:20,820
Please, don't waste it!

408
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:28,460
Kurea, the girl standing in front of you

409
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:29,920
is your new friend.

410
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:37,160
Is this for real?

411
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:39,100
She's my new friend?

412
00:23:12,016 --> 00:23:19,016
I think I got here a little early.

413
00:23:19,016 --> 00:23:22,016
Still, I'm gonna have to fix this place fast.

414
00:23:22,016 --> 00:23:27,016
The flower bed has to be packed full of flowers again before Kureha's birthday.

415
00:23:27,016 --> 00:23:30,016
Well, good morning, Sumika.

416
00:23:37,016 --> 00:23:39,016
Such a lovely morning.

417
00:23:39,016 --> 00:23:41,016
And I'm practically starving.

418
00:23:41,016 --> 00:23:43,016
Mitsuko, is that you?

419
00:23:50,016 --> 00:23:53,016
That day, I committed a serious crime.

420
00:23:53,016 --> 00:23:55,016
I am a criminal bear.

